#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124513 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124322 :question/id #uuid "521cc49e-dddb-5add-b619-18e2785049f8" :question/math-academy-id "e-5432" :question/problem "Find the standard matrix that represents  the  linear  transformation $\\mathbf{T},$ where\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]}\n\\longrightarrow \n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}4 y - 5 x \\\\ y + 3 x\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "First, rewrite the order of the variables in the usual way:\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{T}:\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]}\n\\longrightarrow \n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 5 x + 4 y \\\\ 3 x + y\\end{array} \\right]}\n$$\n\nWe require a $2\\times 2$ matrix ${T}$ such that\n$$\n{T}\\cdot\n    {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]}\n    =\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 5 x + 4 y \\\\ 3 x + y\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$\n\nNotice that\n$$\n{\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}- 5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{array} \\right]}\n\t\\cdot\n    {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}x \\\\ y\\end{array} \\right]}\n    =\n    {\\left[ \\begin{array}{c}- 5 x + 4 y \\\\ 3 x + y\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the matrix which represents the linear transformation $\\mathbf{T}$ is\n$$\nT=\n    {\\left[ \\begin{array}{cc}- 5 & 4 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{array} \\right]}.\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b2776554-94ce-5c25-b838-16fdfceddb1c" :knowledge-point/level-coverage [{:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186125112 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ba773fe1-97fa-574f-b04e-2b7b7c39eaf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 1 & -3 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186123273} {:answer/id #uuid "cf6ed53c-2d90-5472-9895-9440dbdde76b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value